window.NTI=window.NTI||{};(window.NTI.docs=window.NTI.docs||{})["terraform-04-level-2-variables-types-defaults-cli-flags-tfvars-tf-var-env"]={"html":"<p>{/* MIGRATED from: D:\\NTI Courses Master Folder\\TerraformMaster Folder\\Terraform\\level2\\01-variables-outputs.md (2026-09-07)\nCourse metadata: course=terraform | level=2 | difficulty=Intermediate→Advanced\nNote: source had two \"## 9. Function catalog\" headers back-to-back; merged into one during migration. */}</p>\n<h1 id=\"level-2-variables-types-defaults-cli-flags-tfvars-tf-var-env-complete-guide\">Level 2 — Variables: Types, Defaults, CLI Flags, .tfvars, TF_VAR_ Env — Complete Guide</h1>\n<p>Companion to <a href=\"/courses/terraform/level1/workflow/\">Core Workflow</a> (§2 variables) and <a href=\"/courses/terraform/level1/modules/\">Modules</a> (consume <code>source</code>/<code>version</code> + <code>module.Z</code> outputs). This file drills the variable-passing pipeline end-to-end with every mechanism tested.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-variable-declaration-types-full-reference\">1. Variable declaration types (full reference)</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-attribute\">variable</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env\"</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span>        = string          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># primitive</span>\n  default     = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev\"</span>           <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># optional fallback; omitting makes it REQUIRED</span>\n  description = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev/staging/prod\"</span>\n  validation {\n    <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">condition</span>     = contains([<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"staging\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span>], var.env)\n    error_message = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"must be dev/staging/prod\"</span>\n  }\n}\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"count\"</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span>        = number\n  default     = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n  validation { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">condition</span> = var.count &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &amp;&amp; var.count &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>; <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">error_message</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"1..10\"</span> }\n}\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"enabled\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = bool; <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = <span class=\"hljs-literal\">true</span> }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"tags\"</span>    { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = map(string); <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = {} }\n<span class=\"hljs-attribute\">variable</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"azs\"</span>     { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = list(string); <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = [<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"us-east-1a\"</span>] }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"items\"</span>   { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = set(string); <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = [] }                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># unique, unordered — ideal for for_each</span>\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"pair\"</span>    { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = tuple([string, number]); <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = [<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"web\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] } <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># fixed length, mixed types</span>\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"server\"</span>  { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = object({ <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">name</span> = string, size = number }); <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">name</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"web\"</span>, size = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> } }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"any_fallback\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = any; <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = null }   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># avoid when you can; no validation</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Type rules: <code>string</code> / <code>number</code> / <code>bool</code> primitives; <code>list(TYPE)</code> ordered + indexable; <code>set(TYPE)</code> unique + unordered (use with <code>for_each</code>, never <code>count</code> — reordering breaks indexes); <code>map(TYPE)</code> string keys; <code>object({k=TYPE})</code> fixed schema; <code>tuple([TYPE...])</code> fixed-length mixed; <code>any</code> skips checking (backward-compat / dynamic fallbacks only).</p>\n<p>Three declaration attributes most guides skip:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\">variable \"db_password\" {\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span>      = string\n  sensitive = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">true</span>    # hides <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> plan/apply output <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">AND</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> `terraform output` unless forced\n  # NOTE: still stored PLAINTEXT <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> state — sensitive ≠ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">encrypted</span> (see state backend risks)\n}\nvariable \"env\" {\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span>     = string\n  nullable = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">false</span>    # <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">passing</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">null</span> falls back <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">to</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">instead</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">of</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">null</span> (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">true</span> = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">null</span> allowed)\n}\nvariable \"token\" {\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span>      = string\n  ephemeral = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">true</span>    # never persisted <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">to</span> state <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> plan files — <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> secrets passed <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">to</span> provisioners/providers\n  # requires recent Terraform; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">check</span> required_version <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">before</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">using</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Multiple <code>validation</code> blocks are allowed (all must pass) — split complex rules for readable errors:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\">variable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"cidr\"</span> {\n  type = string\n  validation { condition = <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">can</span>(<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">cidrhost</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.cidr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)); error_message = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"must be valid CIDR\"</span> }\n  validation { condition = <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">tonumber</span>(<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">split</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.cidr)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span>; error_message = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prefix must be /24 or larger (smaller number)\"</span> }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"2-default-values-when-required-when-optional-trap-patterns\">2. Default values — when required, when optional, trap patterns</h2>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Pattern</th>\n<th>When used</th>\n<th>Risk</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>default = \"x\"</code></td>\n<td>study / dev (fast start)</td>\n<td>someone forgets to override for prod</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>no <code>default</code> (required)</td>\n<td>prod / critical inputs (env, region, count)</td>\n<td><code>plan</code> fails with prompt → CI breaks if env vars missing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>default = null</code> + conditional resource (<code>count = var.create ? 1 : 0</code>)</td>\n<td>optional resources (bastion host, diagnostics)</td>\n<td><code>null</code> with wrong type causes confusing errors — prefer <code>bool</code> + <code>count</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>default = {}</code> (map) then <code>merge(var.tags, local.tags)</code></td>\n<td>tags accumulation</td>\n<td><code>null</code> default for map + <code>merge</code> = error; <code>default = {}</code> safe</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nullable = false</code> + <code>default</code></td>\n<td>caller may pass explicit null (CI templates) but you want the default</td>\n<td>without it, null propagates and breaks <code>merge</code>/<code>for_each</code> downstream</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Safe production pattern:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-title\">variable</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env\"</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span>        = string</span>\n  description = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"REQUIRED: dev / staging / prod\"</span>\n  # <span class=\"hljs-type\">NO</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> → forces caller to provide (<span class=\"hljs-title\">env</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">file</span>, <span class=\"hljs-type\">CLI</span>, <span class=\"hljs-title\">or</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">TF_VAR_</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">env</span> — <span class=\"hljs-title\">never</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">silent</span>)\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Trap demo (run once, remember forever):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\">variable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"tags\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">map</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = null }  # trap: merge(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.tags, {...}) → Error: null value\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"tags\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">map</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = {} }    # safe: merge works, zero tags = empty <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">map</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"3-passing-variables-7-mechanisms-true-precedence-order\">3. Passing variables — 7 mechanisms, true precedence order</h2>\n<p>Terraform's documented load order, lowest → highest (later wins). The old version of this file omitted <code>*.auto.tfvars</code> — corrected here:</p>\n<pre><code>lowest:  TF_VAR_* env vars\n         ↓  terraform.tfvars <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>+ terraform.tfvars.json if present<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>\n         ↓  *.auto.tfvars / *.auto.tfvars.json <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>lexical filename order<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>\nhighest: -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"k=v\"</span> / -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"x.tfvars\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>command-line order, later flag wins<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>\nfallback: `default` <span class=\"hljs-type\">in</span> declaration <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>used only when nothing above provides <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">a</span> value<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"a-cli-flags-var-var-file-highest-priority\">A — CLI flags (<code>-var</code> / <code>-var-file</code>, highest priority)</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">terraform apply -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env=prod\"</span> -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"count=3\"</span>\nterraform apply -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/prod.tfvars -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/extra.tfvars  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># merge: last file wins per key</span>\nterraform plan -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env=dev\"</span> -out=tfplan &amp;&amp; terraform apply tfplan   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># reviewed == executed</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Rule: <code>-var-file</code> for environments (<code>env/dev.tfvars</code>, <code>env/prod.tfvars</code>); <code>-var</code> for quick one-off tests. Never put secrets in <code>.tfvars</code>; dummy/default values only.</p>\n<h3 id=\"b-environment-variables-tf-var-lowest-file-level-priority-but-ci-s-favorite\">B — Environment variables (<code>TF_VAR_*</code>, lowest file-level priority but CI's favorite)</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">export</span> TF_VAR_env=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">export</span> TF_VAR_count=5\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">export</span> TF_VAR_region=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"us-east-1\"</span>\nterraform apply   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># picks these up automatically; no file changes needed</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Windows (PowerShell): <code>$env:TF_VAR_env = \"prod\"</code>; git-bash: <code>export TF_VAR_env=prod</code>.\nTypes via env: everything arrives as STRING — <code>TF_VAR_count=5</code> auto-converts to number, but complex types need HCL syntax: <code>TF_VAR_tags='{\"Env\":\"prod\"}'</code>, <code>TF_VAR_azs='[\"a\",\"b\"]'</code>. Quoting mistakes here are the #1 CI variable bug.\nBest for CI: pipeline sets <code>TF_VAR_*</code>; no file mounts, no <code>.tfvars</code> secrets in artifacts.</p>\n<h3 id=\"c-terraform-tfvars-auto-loaded-no-flag-needed\">C — <code>terraform.tfvars</code> (auto-loaded, no flag needed)</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># terraform.tfvars (loaded by every plan/apply automatically)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">env</span>             <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">count</span>           <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> 2\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">region</span>          <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"us-east-1\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">instance_type</span>   <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"t3.micro\"</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Best for: single-dev laptop. Dangerous for multi-dev (everyone overwrites each other's file). Solution: rename per person (<code>user.tfvars</code>) and use <code>-var-file=user.tfvars</code>. NEVER commit real secrets here — gitignore it and commit <code>terraform.tfvars.example</code> instead:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># terraform.tfvars.example (COMMIT this; copy to terraform.tfvars, fill real values)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">env</span>           <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">db_password</span>   <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"CHANGEME\"</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"d-terraform-tfvars-json-same-auto-load-slot-json-syntax\">D — <code>terraform.tfvars.json</code> (same auto-load slot, JSON syntax)</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-json\"><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"env\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"count\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"tags\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"Project\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">:</span><span class=\"hljs-string\">\"terraform-study\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">}</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Best for: CI that writes JSON config files (Kubernetes ConfigMap-style generation). If BOTH <code>.tfvars</code> and <code>.tfvars.json</code> exist, both load (json after) — avoid having both; pick one.</p>\n<h3 id=\"e-auto-tfvars-auto-loaded-lexical-order-the-missing-mechanism\">E — <code>*.auto.tfvars</code> (auto-loaded, lexical order — the missing mechanism)</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/\n  base.auto.tfvars    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># env = \"dev\", count = 1        (loads first: 'b' &lt; 'o')</span>\n  override.auto.tfvars <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># count = 3                     (loads second, wins for count)</span>\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">terraform apply   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># no flags — both files auto-load, override wins per key</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Use for: layered config (base + per-developer/per-feature overlay) without touching CLI. Trap: a forgotten <code>*.auto.tfvars</code> silently overrides your <code>-var-file</code> expectations — <code>grep -r auto.tfvars</code> when values surprise you. (CLI <code>-var</code> still beats all auto files.)</p>\n<h3 id=\"f-backend-config-backend-block-only-not-variables-tf-vars\">F — <code>-backend-config</code> (backend block ONLY — not <code>variables.tf</code> vars)</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">terraform init -backend-config=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env/dev.hcl\"</span>   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># applies ONLY to backend block args</span>\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># env/dev.hcl</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">bucket</span> <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"my-study-tfstate-12345\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">key</span>    <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev/terraform.tfstate\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attr\">region</span> <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"us-east-1\"</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Cleanest multi-env backend isolation: <code>key</code> per file, no code-level variables in the backend block (backend blocks can't use <code>var.*</code> — literals or <code>-backend-config</code> only, see <a href=\"/courses/terraform/level1/state-backend/\">State Backend</a>).</p>\n<h3 id=\"g-default-fallback-when-nothing-above-provides-a-value\">G — <code>default</code> (fallback when nothing above provides a value)</h3>\n<p>Missing <code>default</code> + nothing provided = interactive prompt (breaks CI). Production rule: every CI-required variable has a non-empty <code>default</code> OR is guaranteed via <code>TF_VAR_*</code> / <code>.tfvars</code> / <code>-var-file</code> in the pipeline.</p>\n<p>Precedence proof lab (run once):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">export</span> TF_VAR_env=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"from-env\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">echo</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">'env = \"from-tfvars\"'</span> &gt; terraform.tfvars\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">echo</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">'env = \"from-auto\"'</span> &gt; z.auto.tfvars\nterraform plan -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">'env=from-cli'</span> -out=t.plan   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># winner: from-cli</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">rm</span> z.auto.tfvars terraform.tfvars; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">unset</span> TF_VAR_env\nterraform plan                                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># falls back to default (or prompts if none)</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"4-variables-expressions-combined-one-complex-example\">4. Variables + expressions combined (one complex example)</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\">locals {\n  # <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Derive</span> from variables, not hardcoded\n  common_tags = <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">merge</span>(\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.tags,\n    {\n      <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Env</span>     = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.env\n      <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Project</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"terraform-study\"</span>\n      <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Level</span>   = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"2\"</span>         # variables + modules guides = level <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    }\n  )\n  subnets = [\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.azs : <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">cidrsubnet</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.cidr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>, k + (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.env == <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span> ? <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> : <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>))\n  ]  # production offset to avoid overlap <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">with</span> study ranges\n  node_names = [\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.count) : <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">format</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"%s-node-%02d\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.project, i)\n  ]\n  # map form: name → config, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> for_each <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">with</span> per-node differences\n  nodes = {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.count) : <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">format</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"%s-node-%02d\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.project, i) =&gt; {\n      az   = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.azs[i % <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">length</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.azs)]   # round-robin <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">AZs</span>\n      tier = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.env == <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span> ? <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"t3.small\"</span> : <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"t3.micro\"</span>\n    }\n  }\n}\nresource <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"aws_instance\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"cluster\"</span> {\n  for_each      = local.nodes          # stable keys: removing node-<span class=\"hljs-number\">01</span> kills only node-<span class=\"hljs-number\">01</span>\n  ami           = data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id\n  instance_type = each.value.tier\n  tags          = <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">merge</span>(local.common_tags, { <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Name</span> = each.key, AZ = each.value.az })\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Expression reference used: <code>for</code> (list + map comprehension), <code>range()</code>, <code>%</code> modulo, <code>cidrsubnet</code>, <code>format()</code>, <code>merge()</code>, ternary, <code>each.key</code>/<code>each.value</code>, <code>length()</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-outputs-export-sensitive-depends-on-chaining\">5. Outputs — export, sensitive, depends_on, chaining</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># outputs.tf</span>\noutput <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"vpc_id\"</span>   { value = aws_vpc.main.id }\noutput <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"vpc_cidr\"</span> { value = aws_vpc.main.cidr_block }\n\noutput <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db_password\"</span> {\n  value     = aws_db_instance.default.password\n  sensitive = true   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># hidden from CLI output; STILL plaintext in state (see state backend risks)</span>\n}\n\noutput <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"alb_dns\"</span> {\n  value      = aws_lb.app.dns_name\n  depends_on = [aws_lb_listener.front]  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># don't report DNS until listener is attached</span>\n}\n\noutput <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"cluster\"</span> {\n  value = { for k, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">inst </span>in aws_instance.cluster : k =&gt; { id = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">inst.id, </span>ip = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">inst.public_ip </span>} }\n  description = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"name → {id, ip} map for inventory/ansible\"</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Reading outputs: <code>terraform output</code> (all), <code>terraform output -json | jq .vpc_id.value</code> (CI), <code>terraform output -raw vpc_id</code> (scripts). Cross-config reads: <code>data \"terraform_remote_state\"</code> (same backend family) or module outputs <code>module.vpc.vpc_id</code> (preferred — see <a href=\"/courses/terraform/level1/modules/\">Modules</a>). Never <code>terraform output</code> secrets into logs; pipe to a secret store.</p>\n<h2 id=\"6-variables-tf-file-patterns-copy-ready\">6. <code>variables.tf</code> file patterns (copy-ready)</h2>\n<p>Pattern A — study (defaults for speed):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\">variable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env\"</span>    { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">string</span>; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"dev\"</span> }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"count\"</span>  { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">number</span>; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"region\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">string</span>; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"us-east-1\"</span> }\n</code></pre>\n<p>Pattern B — production (required, validated):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\">variable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env\"</span>           { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>; validation { condition = contains([<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"staging\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span>], <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.env); error_message = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"staging|prod only\"</span> } }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"count\"</span>         { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = number; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>; validation { condition = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.count &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> &amp;&amp; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.count &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>; error_message = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"2..10 for HA\"</span> } }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"instance_type\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>; validation { condition = can(regex(<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"^t[23]\\\\.\"</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.instance_type)) || <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.instance_type == <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"t3.micro\"</span>; error_message = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"t2/t3 family only\"</span> } }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"tags\"</span>          { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">map</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span> = { Env = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod\"</span> } }\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db_password\"</span>   { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = <span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>; sensitive = <span class=\"hljs-literal\">true</span> }  # no <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span>: must come from Vault/CI secret, never tfvars\n</code></pre>\n<p>Rule: study = <code>default</code> + loose validation; prod = required vars + strict validation + secrets from Vault/SSM/CI (<code>TF_VAR_</code> from secret store), never committed files.</p>\n<h2 id=\"7-end-to-end-wired-lab-all-four-files-floci-ready\">7. End-to-end wired lab (all four files, Floci-ready)</h2>\n<pre><code>lab-vars/\n  versions.tf     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># pins (see workflow versions section)</span>\n  variables.tf    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># §1 + §2 patterns</span>\n  main.tf         <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># locals (§4) + 1 local_file resource per node name (no cloud needed)</span>\n  outputs.tf      <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># §5 patterns</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/dev.tfvars  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># env=\"dev\" count=2</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/prod.tfvars <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># env=\"prod\" count=3</span>\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">cd</span> lab-vars &amp;&amp; terraform init\nterraform plan -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/dev.tfvars    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># expect: 2 to add</span>\nterraform apply -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/dev.tfvars\nterraform output -json | jq keys\nTF_VAR_count=1 terraform plan -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/dev.tfvars  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># env var loses to file? NO — file is -var-file (CLI),</span>\n                                                         <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># CLI beats TF_VAR_: count stays 2. Proof of §3 order.</span>\nterraform destroy -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/dev.tfvars\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"9-function-catalog-the-20-you-will-actually-call-with-when-how-traps\">9. Function catalog — the 20+ you will actually call (with when, how, traps)</h2>\n<p>Grouped by job, each with a runnable shape, when-to-use, and the trap. Test any of them instantly with <code>terraform console</code> (§13).</p>\n<h3 id=\"9-1-string-functions\">9.1 String functions</h3>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th>When to use it</th>\n<th>Trap</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>format(\"node-%02d-%s\", 3, var.env)</code></td>\n<td>printf-style, returns <code>\"node-03-prod\"</code></td>\n<td>zero-padded names (<code>node-01</code>, <code>node-02</code>) and templated IDs (ARN paths, hostnames)</td>\n<td><code>%d</code> for numbers, <code>%s</code> for strings, <code>%02d</code> = pad to 2 digits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>join(\",\", var.azs)</code></td>\n<td>list → single string, returns <code>\"us-east-1a,us-east-1b\"</code></td>\n<td><code>user_data</code> (bash arrays), tag values, comma-separated config</td>\n<td>returns string; to read it back use <code>split</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>split(\",\", \"a,b,c\")</code></td>\n<td>string → list, returns <code>[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]</code></td>\n<td>reverse of join; parsing CI strings (<code>TF_VAR_azs=\"a,b,c\"</code>)</td>\n<td>empty input → <code>[\"\"]</code>, not <code>[]</code> — use <code>length(x[0]) &gt; 0</code> checks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>upper(var.env) / lower(var.env)</code></td>\n<td>case change, returns <code>\"PROD\"</code></td>\n<td>tag normalization (S3 keys case-sensitive; Linux DNS is case-insensitive)</td>\n<td><code>lower()</code> on a list applies to the list, not elements — iterate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>substr(var.project, 0, 8)</code></td>\n<td>substring by start,length</td>\n<td>AWS length limits (IAM role name 64, SG name 255)</td>\n<td>start past string end → \"\"; length 0 → \"\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>replace(var.name, \"_\", \"-\")</code></td>\n<td>string replace, returns <code>\"my-thing\"</code></td>\n<td>sanitize S3/ALB names (S3 rejects underscores in some ops)</td>\n<td>regex NOT supported — for regex use <code>regex(...)</code> or <code>replace</code> in <code>aws_*_policy</code> JSON</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>trimspace(var.input)</code></td>\n<td>strip leading/trailing whitespace</td>\n<td>sanitize CI inputs (templates add a trailing <code>\\n</code> or space)</td>\n<td>doesn't strip inside the string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>regex(\"[^a-z0-9]\", var.name)</code></td>\n<td>match → bool, used with <code>can()</code>/<code>condition</code></td>\n<td>validation: <code>condition = !can(regex(\"[^a-z0-9]\", var.name))</code></td>\n<td>pattern syntax = RE2; remember to escape <code>-</code> at character classes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>regexall(\"[0-9]+\", \"a1b22\")</code></td>\n<td>all matches → list, returns <code>[\"1\",\"22\"]</code></td>\n<td>extract IDs from ARNs; parse log formats</td>\n<td>returns strings, even when they look numeric — <code>tonumber()</code> after</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># Test any in REPL</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">echo</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">'format(\"vpc-%s-%s\", var.project, var.env)'</span> | terraform console -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"project=study\"</span> -var=<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"env=prod\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># → \"vpc-study-prod\"</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"9-2-collection-functions\">9.2 Collection functions</h3>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th>When to use it</th>\n<th>Trap</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>merge(var.tags, { Env = var.env })</code></td>\n<td>deep-merge maps, right wins on key collision</td>\n<td>combine caller tags + mandatory tags</td>\n<td>only top-level keys — nested maps NOT deep-merged</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>merge([for m in var.tag_sets : m]...)</code></td>\n<td>spread list-of-maps into merge args</td>\n<td>merging N variable maps when count is dynamic</td>\n<td>the <code>...</code> is mandatory; without it you pass a list as one arg and get an error</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>concat(var.azs_a, var.azs_b)</code></td>\n<td>ordered combine, keeps duplicates</td>\n<td>join caller AZs + forced AZs, layers of resources</td>\n<td>duplicates preserved — use <code>distinct()</code> after if needed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>distinct(concat(var.a, var.b))</code></td>\n<td>dedupe (any type, hash by value)</td>\n<td>dedupe after concat, normalize user input</td>\n<td>O(n) cost — fine for n &lt; 100, careful for n &gt; 1000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>flatten([[\"a\",\"b\"],[\"c\"]])</code></td>\n<td>nested → flat, returns <code>[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]</code></td>\n<td><code>for_each</code> from a list-of-lists config (multi-AZ groups)</td>\n<td>flattens one level only — double-nested needs two <code>flatten()</code> calls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>keys(var.amis) / values(var.amis)</code></td>\n<td>map → list</td>\n<td>iterate map for <code>for_each</code>; pair with <code>zipmap</code></td>\n<td>order = lexicographic by key (deterministic), not insertion order</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>lookup(var.amis, var.region, \"fallback\")</code></td>\n<td>map get with default</td>\n<td>AMI per region with fallback to a default image</td>\n<td>no error on miss — perfect for <code>data \"aws_ami\"</code> lookups</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>contains(var.azs, \"us-east-1a\")</code></td>\n<td>membership → bool</td>\n<td>validation <code>condition = contains([...], var.az)</code>; gate a resource</td>\n<td>exact match — <code>contains([\"us-east-1A\"], \"us-east-1a\")</code> = false</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>length(var.azs)</code></td>\n<td>list/map/string → number</td>\n<td><code>count</code> / <code>for_each</code> sizing; modulo</td>\n<td>on <code>null</code> → <code>Error: null</code> — guard with <code>coalesce(var.x, [])</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>element(var.azs, count.index)</code></td>\n<td>round-robin by index</td>\n<td>legacy pattern; prefer <code>var.azs[count.index % length(var.azs)]</code></td>\n<td><code>element</code> panics on out-of-range; modulo is safer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>slice(var.azs, 0, 2)</code></td>\n<td>first N (or middle range)</td>\n<td>cap to multi-AZ count: <code>slice(var.azs, 0, var.max_azs)</code></td>\n<td>end &gt; length → just returns up to end</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setproduct(var.tiers, var.azs)</code></td>\n<td>cartesian pairs → list of lists</td>\n<td>every (tier × AZ) combination for matrix testing</td>\n<td>one resource per pair can blow up; combine with <code>length() &gt; N</code> guard</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>zipmap(var.names, var.ips)</code></td>\n<td>two lists → map</td>\n<td>build inventory: <code>for_each = zipmap(vm_names, vm_ips)</code></td>\n<td>lists must be same length — mismatched → <code>Error: length mismatch</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"># <span class=\"hljs-type\">Real</span> pattern: merge N variable maps (caller tags + per-resource tags + mandatory)\nlocals {\n  base_tags    = { ManagedBy = \"terraform\", <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">Level</span> = \"2\" }\n  caller_tags  = var.tags              # may be empty map\n  region_tags  = { Region = data.aws_region.<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">current</span>.name }\n  all_tags     = merge(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.base_tags, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.caller_tags, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.region_tags)\n}\n# <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">Conflict</span> resolution <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">order</span>: last wins → region_tags overrides base_tags <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">on</span> Region key\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"9-3-numbers-amp-cidr\">9.3 Numbers &amp; CIDR</h3>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th>When to use it</th>\n<th>Trap</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>max(var.min_nodes, 2) / min(var.max_nodes, 10)</code></td>\n<td>clamp</td>\n<td>hard-floor a minimum: <code>max(var.count, 2)</code> for HA</td>\n<td><code>min(5, 10) = 5</code> — sanity check, not enforcement (use validation for that)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ceil(var.spot_ratio * 100) / floor(...)</code></td>\n<td>round up/down</td>\n<td>percentages without floats leaking (count of spot instances = ceil(total * ratio))</td>\n<td><code>ceil(2.0) = 2</code>, not 3 — int floats first</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cidrsubnet(var.cidr, 8, k)</code></td>\n<td>subnet of <code>var.cidr</code> widened by 8 bits, netnum <code>k</code></td>\n<td>lay out subnets: <code>cidrsubnet(\"10.0.0.0/16\", 8, 0)</code> → <code>10.0.0.0/24</code></td>\n<td>newbits = the size diff (16→24 = 8)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cidrhost(\"10.0.1.0/24\", 5)</code></td>\n<td>5th host IP → <code>10.0.1.5</code></td>\n<td>NAT gateway IPs, manual DNS records</td>\n<td><code>cidrhost(cidr, 0)</code> = network address (<code>.0</code>); <code>cidrhost(cidr, -1)</code> = broadcast (<code>.255</code> in /24)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cidrnetmask(\"10.0.0.0/16\")</code></td>\n<td>→ <code>\"255.255.0.0\"</code></td>\n<td>generate firewall rule strings for legacy config</td>\n<td>only IPv4; IPv6 needs different tooling</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cidrsubnets(\"10.0.0.0/16\", 4, 4, 4, 4)</code></td>\n<td>split one CIDR into N</td>\n<td>\"give me 4 /18s from a /16\"</td>\n<td>up to 4 netmasks per call — chain for more</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cidrsubnet_newbits</code> calc</td>\n<td>mental: <code>target_size = source_size + newbits</code></td>\n<td>for <code>count</code> of N subnets, <code>newbits = ceil(log2(N))</code></td>\n<td>off-by-one: 5 subnets need <code>newbits=3</code> (8 slots)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"># <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span> public + <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span> private + <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span> db subnets from /<span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>, <span class=\"hljs-type\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span> AZs\nlocals {\n  pub    = [for k <span class=\"hljs-type\">in</span> range<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span> : cidrsubnet<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>var.cidr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>, k<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>]        # .<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span>\n  priv   = [for k <span class=\"hljs-type\">in</span> range<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span> : cidrsubnet<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>var.cidr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>, k + <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>]  # .<span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">11</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span>\n  db     = [for k <span class=\"hljs-type\">in</span> range<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span> : cidrsubnet<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>var.cidr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>, k + <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>]  # .<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">21</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">22</span>/<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span>\n  # Reverse: <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span> IPs reserved per subnet <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>.<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span> .<span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>, so /<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> = <span class=\"hljs-number\">251</span> usable\n  gateway_ips = [for cidr <span class=\"hljs-type\">in</span> local.pub : cidrhost<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">(</span>cidr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">)</span>]       # AWS reserves .<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"9-4-safety-amp-defensive\">9.4 Safety &amp; defensive</h3>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th>When to use it</th>\n<th>Trap</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>try(var.optional_obj.attr, \"default\")</code></td>\n<td>dig without crash</td>\n<td>optional nested configs (module inputs that may be missing)</td>\n<td><code>try</code> doesn't short-circuit errors inside the success path — test the value too</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>can(regex(\"^t[23]\\\\.\", var.instance_type))</code></td>\n<td>boolean test</td>\n<td>validation <code>condition</code> for shape-checking</td>\n<td>don't use <code>can()</code> outside validation — uses the value and may hide real errors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>can(cidrhost(var.cidr, 0))</code></td>\n<td>\"is this a CIDR?\"</td>\n<td>validation of CIDR-shaped input</td>\n<td>cheap and bulletproof — pair with <code>cidrsubnet</code> to also require it to be subnettable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>coalesce(var.a, var.b, \"fallback\")</code></td>\n<td>first non-null/non-empty</td>\n<td>override chains (CLI &gt; tfvars &gt; default)</td>\n<td>works on primitives only; <code>coalescelist</code> for lists</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>coalescelist(var.a, var.b)</code></td>\n<td>first non-empty list</td>\n<td><code>for_each = coalescelist(var.optional, [])</code> — never <code>null</code></td>\n<td>empty list <code>[]</code> counts as \"exists\" — use <code>length() &gt; 0</code> to differentiate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>one(aws_instance.maybe[*].id)</code></td>\n<td>exactly-one-or-null</td>\n<td><code>count = 0/1</code> resources; returns the value or <code>null</code></td>\n<td>panics on &gt;1 — use <code>one()</code> only when you KNOW the cardinality</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>tostring(var.count) / tonumber(var.str)</code></td>\n<td>type conversion</td>\n<td><code>TF_VAR_count=5</code> arrives as string; tags need strings</td>\n<td><code>tonumber(\"\")</code> → error — guard with <code>try()</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>jsonencode(var.tags) / jsondecode(var.json)</code></td>\n<td>serialize/parse JSON</td>\n<td><code>user_data</code> (cloud-init), IAM policies, ECS task definitions</td>\n<td><code>jsondecode</code> of bad JSON = error — wrap in <code>try</code> for optional</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>yamlencode(var.map) / yamldecode(var.yaml)</code></td>\n<td>YAML ser/deser</td>\n<td>k8s manifests (<code>kubernetes_manifest</code>), Ansible inventory</td>\n<td><code>yamlencode</code> of a map preserves insertion order, not alphabetic — be aware</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>base64encode(var.script) / base64decode(...)</code></td>\n<td>b64 transport</td>\n<td>user_data payload, IAM policy body, secrets in transit</td>\n<td><code>base64decode</code> of invalid = error</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sensitive(var.pw)</code></td>\n<td>mark sensitive mid-expression</td>\n<td>outputs of derived values that contain secrets</td>\n<td>the value is still IN state; sensitive ≠ encrypted</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nonsensitive(var.maybe)</code></td>\n<td>UNSAFE reverse</td>\n<td>only for debugging, never commit</td>\n<td>exposes secrets in plan output — biggest rookie mistake</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>timestamp()</code></td>\n<td>now (RFC3339)</td>\n<td><strong>never in resources</strong> (non-idempotent — drift on every plan)</td>\n<td>only in <code>ignore_changes</code> lifecycles for rotation triggers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>uuid()</code></td>\n<td>random UUID</td>\n<td>same warning — never as a resource attribute</td>\n<td>if you need a stable suffix, use <code>random_id</code> and pin via <code>keepers</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"># <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">try</span>() + coalesce + <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">can</span>() combined — the <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"tolerant lookup\"</span> pattern\nlocals {\n  region_ami = <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">try</span>(\n    <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">lookup</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span>.ami_overrides, data.aws_region.current.name, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">null</span>),  # <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">try</span> the override\n    data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id,                                          # fall back to data source\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ami-fallback\"</span>                                                  # last-resort <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">default</span>\n  )\n}\n# <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Three</span>-tier: caller override → data lookup → string fallback. <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Crashes</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">on</span> NONE of them.\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"9-5-quick-reference-the-cheat-sheet\">9.5 Quick reference (the cheat sheet)</h3>\n<pre><code>STRING  format, join, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">split</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">upper</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">lower</span>, substr, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">replace</span>, trimspace, regex, regexall\nLIST    concat, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">distinct</span>, flatten, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">length</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">contains</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">slice</span>, setproduct, element\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">MAP</span>     keys, values, merge, lookup, zipmap\nNUM     <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">ceil</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">floor</span>\nCIDR    cidrsubnet, cidrhost, cidrnetmask, cidrsubnets\nSAFE    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">try</span>, can, coalesce, coalescelist, one\nTYPE    tostring, tonumber, tobool, tolist, toset, tomap\nENCODE  jsonencode, jsondecode, yamlencode, yamldecode, base64encode, base64decode\nRUNTIME sensitive, nonsensitive (carefully!), <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">timestamp</span> (avoid!), uuid (avoid!)\n</code></pre>\n<p>Rule: prefer <code>length()</code>/<code>contains()</code>/<code>lookup()</code> with default over <code>try()</code> when you can — they're cheaper to read.</p>\n<h2 id=\"10-dynamic-blocks-driven-by-variables-sgs-without-repetition\">10. Dynamic blocks driven by variables (SGs without repetition)</h2>\n<p>The professional answer to \"N ingress rules from a variable\":</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">variable</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ingress_rules\"</span> {\n  type <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= list(object({</span>\n    desc  <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= string</span>\n    from  <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= number</span>\n    to    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= number</span>\n    proto <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= string</span>\n    cidrs <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= list(string)</span>\n  }))\n  default <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= [</span>\n    { desc <span class=\"hljs-comment\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"http\"</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">,  from = 80, to = 80, proto =</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"tcp\"</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">, cidrs = [</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"0.0.0.0/0\"</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">] },</span>\n    { desc <span class=\"hljs-comment\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"https\"</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">, from = 443, to = 443, proto =</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"tcp\"</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">, cidrs = [</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"0.0.0.0/0\"</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">] },</span>\n  ]\n}\nresource <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"aws_security_group\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"web\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">{</span>\n  name   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"web-sg\"</span>\n  vpc_id <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= aws_vpc.main.id</span>\n  dynamic <span class=\"hljs-comment\">\"ingress\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">{</span>\n    for_each <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= var.ingress_rules</span>\n    content <span class=\"hljs-comment\">{</span>\n      description <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= ingress.value.desc</span>\n      from_port   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= ingress.value.from</span>\n      to_port     <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= ingress.value.to</span>\n      protocol    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= ingress.value.proto</span>\n      cidr_blocks <span class=\"hljs-comment\">= ingress.value.cidrs</span>\n    }\n  }\n  egress <span class=\"hljs-comment\">{ from_port = 0</span>; to_port = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; protocol = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"-1\"</span>; cidr_blocks = [<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"0.0.0.0/0\"</span>] }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Add a rule = append one object to <code>.tfvars</code>, zero HCL edits. Same pattern drives <code>aws_lb_listener</code> actions, <code>ingress</code> on ALB SGs, IAM policy statements.</p>\n<h2 id=\"11-secrets-end-to-end-variables-stay-clean\">11. Secrets end-to-end (variables stay clean)</h2>\n<p>Rule hardened: secrets NEVER ride variables from files. Three production shapes:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># A — SSM Parameter Store (AWS-native, no extra infra)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-attribute\">data</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"aws_ssm_parameter\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db_pw\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">name</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/${var.env}/db/password\"</span>; <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">with_decryption</span> = <span class=\"hljs-literal\">true</span> }\nresource <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"aws_db_instance\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"main\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">password</span> = data.aws_ssm_parameter.db_pw.value ... }\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># variable carries only the PATH, never the secret:</span>\nvariable <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db_pw_path\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">type</span> = string; <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">default</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/dev/db/password\"</span> }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># B — Secrets Manager (rotation-friendly)</span>\ndata <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">secret_id</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"prod/db\"</span> }\nlocals { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">db_creds</span> = jsondecode(data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db.secret_string) }\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># use local.db_creds.username / .password — marked sensitive at the output (§5)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># C — Vault (multi-cloud / teams with Vault)</span>\ndata <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"vault_kv_secret_v2\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">mount</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"kv\"</span>; <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">name</span> = <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"db/prod\"</span> }\nresource <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"aws_db_instance\"</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"main\"</span> { <span class=\"hljs-attribute\">password</span> = data.vault_kv_secret_v2.db.data[<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"password\"</span>] ... }\n</code></pre>\n<p>CI shape: pipeline fetches secret → <code>TF_VAR_</code> ONLY if the runner is trusted AND masked in logs; better: pass the secret's PATH/ARN as the variable, let Terraform read the value via data source at apply time. State still holds plaintext — bucket encryption + tight IAM is non-negotiable.</p>\n<h2 id=\"12-workspace-aware-variable-selection-one-codebase-n-envs\">12. Workspace-aware variable selection (one codebase, N envs)</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-hcl\"># envs.tf — <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">no</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">new</span> files per env, selection <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">by</span> workspace <span class=\"hljs-type\">name</span>\nlocals {\n  env = terraform.workspace == \"default\" ? \"dev\" : terraform.workspace\n  sizing = {\n    dev     = { count = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = \"t3.micro\" }\n    staging = { count = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = \"t3.small\" }\n    prod    = { count = <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> = \"t3.small\" }\n  }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">current</span> = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.sizing[<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.env]\n}\nresource \"aws_instance\" \"cluster\" {\n  count         = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">current</span>.count\n  instance_type = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">current</span>.<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span>\n  tags          = { Env = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">local</span>.env }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">terraform workspace new dev &amp;&amp; terraform apply      <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># 1× micro</span>\nterraform workspace new prod &amp;&amp; terraform apply     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># 3× small, isolated state</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Trade-off vs <code>-var-file</code>: workspaces hide the env in invisible state — <code>terraform workspace show</code> before EVERY apply. Teams usually prefer explicit <code>-var-file</code> (visible in the command) + separate keys/buckets.</p>\n<h2 id=\"13-debugging-variables-console-tf-log-plan-targeted\">13. Debugging variables (<code>console</code>, <code>TF_LOG</code>, plan-targeted)</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># terraform console — REPL for expressions (fastest function/variable lab, no apply)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">echo</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">'format(\"node-%02d-%s\", 3, \"prod\")'</span> | terraform console        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># \"node-03-prod\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">echo</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">'cidrsubnet(\"10.0.0.0/16\", 8, 10)'</span> | terraform console        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># \"10.0.10.0/24\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">echo</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">'merge({\"a\"=1}, {\"b\"=2})'</span> | terraform console                 <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># {\"a\"=1,\"b\"=2}</span>\nterraform console -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/prod.tfvars                         <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># console WITH your real vars loaded</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># see exactly which value a variable resolved to (and from where)</span>\nTF_LOG=TRACE terraform plan -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/prod.tfvars 2&gt;&amp;1 | grep -i <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"var\\.env\\|value\"</span>\nterraform plan -var-file=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">env</span>/prod.tfvars -out=t.plan &amp;&amp; terraform show -json t.plan | jq <span class=\"hljs-string\">'.variables'</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"14-error-catalog-exact-messages-fixes\">14. Error catalog (exact messages → fixes)</h2>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Error</th>\n<th>Cause</th>\n<th>Fix</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>No value for required variable</code> + prompt</td>\n<td>no default, nothing provided</td>\n<td>add <code>-var</code> / <code>TF_VAR_</code> / tfvars entry (§3)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Invalid value for input variable: must be dev/staging/prod</code></td>\n<td>validation failed</td>\n<td>pass allowed value; read <code>error_message</code> literally</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>string required, but have number</code> / vice versa</td>\n<td><code>TF_VAR_</code> quoting or tfvars type mismatch</td>\n<td>quote complex env values as HCL (<code>'{\"a\":1}'</code>); check declared <code>type</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>null value is not allowed for...</code> / <code>merge</code> null error</td>\n<td><code>default = null</code> + function needing concrete</td>\n<td><code>nullable = false</code>, or <code>default = {}</code>, or <code>coalesce(var.x, {})</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>reference to undeclared resource / each.key not available</code></td>\n<td><code>each.*</code> outside <code>for_each</code> resource / dynamic content</td>\n<td>scope <code>each</code> correctly; dynamic blocks use block-label (<code>ingress.value</code>), resources use <code>each.value</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>variables not allowed here</code> (backend block)</td>\n<td><code>var.*</code> inside <code>backend \"s3\"</code></td>\n<td>literals or <code>-backend-config</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sensitive value...</code> in plan diff</td>\n<td>sensitive var flows into output/resource attr shown</td>\n<td>expected — mark downstream output <code>sensitive</code>, don't <code>nonsensitive</code> to \"fix\" display</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Inconsistent conditional result types</code></td>\n<td>ternary branches differ (<code>string</code> vs <code>number</code>)</td>\n<td><code>tostring()</code> one branch or align types</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>iteration over null value</code> in <code>for_each</code></td>\n<td>variable null, no default</td>\n<td><code>default = []</code>/<code>{}</code>, or <code>for_each = coalesce(var.x, [])</code> (sets) / <code>var.x != null ? var.x : {}</code> (maps)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2 id=\"15-interview-q-amp-a-expanded\">15. Interview Q&amp;A (expanded)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Precedence order?</strong> <code>-var</code>/<code>-var-file</code> &gt; <code>*.auto.tfvars</code> (lexical) &gt; <code>terraform.tfvars</code> &gt; <code>TF_VAR_*</code> env &gt; <code>default</code>. Prove with the §3 lab.</li>\n<li><strong><code>terraform.tfvars</code> vs <code>*.auto.tfvars</code>?</strong> Former: single conventional file, auto-loaded. Latter: many, layered, lexical merge — overlays without CLI flags.</li>\n<li><strong>Why is my <code>-var-file</code> value ignored?</strong> A later <code>-var</code>/<code>-var-file</code> flag, or you expected file to beat CLI — it never does.</li>\n<li><strong><code>sensitive = true</code> — encrypted?</strong> No. Hidden from output only; state still plaintext. Real secrecy = Vault/SSM + <code>ephemeral</code> where supported.</li>\n<li><strong><code>set</code> vs <code>list</code> for <code>for_each</code>?</strong> Sets (or maps) have stable keys; lists re-index on removal.</li>\n<li><strong>Backend block with variables?</strong> Not allowed — literals or <code>-backend-config</code> files only.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Next: <a href=\"/courses/terraform/level1/modules/\">Modules</a> deep-dive combined with this variables/outputs material, or verified Floci apply execution.</p>\n","toc":[{"id":"level-2-variables-types-defaults-cli-flags-tfvars-tf-var-env-complete-guide","text":"Level 2 — Variables: Types, Defaults, CLI Flags, .tfvars, TF_VAR_ Env — Complete Guide","level":1},{"id":"1-variable-declaration-types-full-reference","text":"1. Variable declaration types (full reference)","level":2},{"id":"2-default-values-when-required-when-optional-trap-patterns","text":"2. Default values — when required, when optional, trap patterns","level":2},{"id":"3-passing-variables-7-mechanisms-true-precedence-order","text":"3. Passing variables — 7 mechanisms, true precedence order","level":2},{"id":"a-cli-flags-var-var-file-highest-priority","text":"A — CLI flags (-var / -var-file, highest priority)","level":3},{"id":"b-environment-variables-tf-var-lowest-file-level-priority-but-ci-s-favorite","text":"B — Environment variables (TF_VAR_*, lowest file-level priority but CI's favorite)","level":3},{"id":"c-terraform-tfvars-auto-loaded-no-flag-needed","text":"C — terraform.tfvars (auto-loaded, no flag needed)","level":3},{"id":"d-terraform-tfvars-json-same-auto-load-slot-json-syntax","text":"D — terraform.tfvars.json (same auto-load slot, JSON syntax)","level":3},{"id":"e-auto-tfvars-auto-loaded-lexical-order-the-missing-mechanism","text":"E — *.auto.tfvars (auto-loaded, lexical order — the missing mechanism)","level":3},{"id":"f-backend-config-backend-block-only-not-variables-tf-vars","text":"F — -backend-config (backend block ONLY — not variables.tf vars)","level":3},{"id":"g-default-fallback-when-nothing-above-provides-a-value","text":"G — default (fallback when nothing above provides a value)","level":3},{"id":"4-variables-expressions-combined-one-complex-example","text":"4. Variables + expressions combined (one complex example)","level":2},{"id":"5-outputs-export-sensitive-depends-on-chaining","text":"5. Outputs — export, sensitive, depends_on, chaining","level":2},{"id":"6-variables-tf-file-patterns-copy-ready","text":"6. variables.tf file patterns (copy-ready)","level":2},{"id":"7-end-to-end-wired-lab-all-four-files-floci-ready","text":"7. End-to-end wired lab (all four files, Floci-ready)","level":2},{"id":"9-function-catalog-the-20-you-will-actually-call-with-when-how-traps","text":"9. Function catalog — the 20+ you will actually call (with when, how, traps)","level":2},{"id":"9-1-string-functions","text":"9.1 String functions","level":3},{"id":"9-2-collection-functions","text":"9.2 Collection functions","level":3},{"id":"9-3-numbers-amp-cidr","text":"9.3 Numbers &amp; CIDR","level":3},{"id":"9-4-safety-amp-defensive","text":"9.4 Safety &amp; defensive","level":3},{"id":"9-5-quick-reference-the-cheat-sheet","text":"9.5 Quick reference (the cheat sheet)","level":3},{"id":"10-dynamic-blocks-driven-by-variables-sgs-without-repetition","text":"10. Dynamic blocks driven by variables (SGs without repetition)","level":2},{"id":"11-secrets-end-to-end-variables-stay-clean","text":"11. Secrets end-to-end (variables stay clean)","level":2},{"id":"12-workspace-aware-variable-selection-one-codebase-n-envs","text":"12. Workspace-aware variable selection (one codebase, N envs)","level":2},{"id":"13-debugging-variables-console-tf-log-plan-targeted","text":"13. Debugging variables (console, TF_LOG, plan-targeted)","level":2},{"id":"14-error-catalog-exact-messages-fixes","text":"14. Error catalog (exact messages → fixes)","level":2},{"id":"15-interview-q-amp-a-expanded","text":"15. Interview Q&amp;A (expanded)","level":2}],"words":2508,"assets":[]};